We can use the AM-GM inequality to find a lower bound for the expression. We have \begin{align*} x^4 + 4y^2 + 4z^4 &= (x^4) + (y^2) + (y^2) + (z^4) + (z^4) \\ &\geq 5 \sqrt[5]{x^4 y^2 y^2 z^4} \\ &= 5 \sqrt[5]{(xyz)^4} \\ &= 5 \sqrt[5]{2^4} \\ &= 5 \cdot 2^{4/5}. \end{align*} Equality occurs when $x^4 = y^2 = z^4$, which implies $x = y = z$. Since $xyz = 2$, we have $x = y = z = \sqrt[3]{2}$. Therefore, the minimum value of the expression is $\boxed{5 \cdot 2^{4/5}}$.The answer is: \boxed{5 \cdot 2^{4/5}}
